claims[100]{question_id,source_id,claim}:
  cal-20261002-s5-001,s1,"Session 3 endorsed the calendar, first-hand observations, mathematics blocks and more."
  cal-20261002-s5-002,s1,"The post was added as a starting draft for the author to edit, and is live."
  cal-20261002-s5-003,s1,Seven engineering visualisations were restyled to the shared style guide.
  cal-20261002-s5-004,s1,The podcast episode is made from 34 #calibrator notes of 2 October.
  cal-20261002-s5-005,s1,The calendar todo is dated 2 October 2026 and is still open.
  cal-20261002-s5-006,s1,Session 4's notes open with a five-point digest.
  cal-20261002-s5-007,s1,The card on the visualisation opened on three days did not name it.
  cal-20261002-s5-008,s1,The token audit has not been briefed to a crewmate; I am still deciding whether to hand it over.
  cal-20261002-s5-009,s1,Agent tooling is taking my mathematics hours this month.
  cal-20261002-s5-010,s1,My review stays at decisions and outcomes; the safeguards I chose are automated.
  cal-20261002-s5-011,s1,"Kun Chen says that when a project runs smoothly he panics, since he is no longer adding value."
  cal-20261002-s5-012,s1,Agent work crowded out time with people this week.
  cal-20261002-s5-013,s1,Session 4 is the third confirmation that I trust automated checks over my own review.
  cal-20261002-s5-014,s1,Posting beamdiag in a public structural-engineering forum is parked until 1 November.
  cal-20261002-s5-015,s1,The spend cap is to be set without looking at September's spend.
  cal-20261002-s5-016,s1,November's étale computation is to be chosen in an October mathematics block.
  cal-20261002-s5-017,s1,"Agent tooling should help me become a better human, not merely replace more tasks."
  cal-20261002-s5-018,s1,Site main received dozens of commits on 1 and 2 October 2026.
  cal-20261002-s5-019,s1,"With an agent writing the code, the author is the checks and balances."
  cal-20261002-s5-020,s1,"Notes an agent writes carry #agent-written, going forward."
  cal-20261002-s5-021,s1,Every dated-todo card in session 4 stayed a note.
  cal-20261002-s5-022,s1,Firstmate's alerts are to be batched into two daily windows.
  cal-20261002-s5-023,s1,"The secret scan found no credentials, only low-severity private paths."
  cal-20261002-s5-024,s1,"Stage B compares checksums, requires HTTP 200 and checks for expected text."
  cal-20261002-s5-025,s1,"cal-20261002-s4-045 resolved true: 26 data/visuals records were added from 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-02."
  cal-20261002-s5-026,s1,Deploys run from a local checkout; the playbook names no lock.
  cal-20261002-s5-027,s1,The site is written mostly for agents.
  cal-20261002-s5-028,s1,Micromanaging an agent's code is a mistake; write down principles that steer all the agents.
  cal-20261002-s5-029,s1,Work an open card asks about is to be held until the card is answered.
  cal-20261002-s5-030,s1,Treat every agent tool as temporary scaffold rebuilt every six months or faster.
  cal-20261002-s5-031,s1,Several todos fall due on 9 and 10 October.
  cal-20261002-s5-032,s1,"I learn mathematics and physics by hand and from textbooks, and structural engineering by building tools."
  cal-20261002-s5-033,s1,Ask what I did this month that I could not do last month.
  cal-20261002-s5-034,s1,Four pasted exports had UTF-8 read as Latin-1; each recording restored the text from the published session.
  cal-20261002-s5-035,s1,The FBD drawer was restyled with the shared visual style guide.
  cal-20261002-s5-036,s1,The first mathematics block goes to the information-cohomology afternoon.
  cal-20261002-s5-037,s1,"The agent curfew moves from midnight to 23:00, enforced by a hook or mod."
  cal-20261002-s5-038,s1,A session-4 card wrongly said the audit had been briefed.
  cal-20261002-s5-039,s1,"For me, a small immediate experiment beats more reading when the uncertainty is empirical."
  cal-20261002-s5-040,s1,Redo the one-loop QED beta function by hand before using the QED laboratory.
  cal-20261002-s5-041,s1,A narrated beamdswitch deck summarises Kun Chen's advice for engineers.
  cal-20261002-s5-042,s1,December is planned for quantum field theory through notes and labs rather than a lecture series.
  cal-20261002-s5-043,s1,Fastener Pattern CG Tracker tracks a fastener pattern's centroid.
  cal-20261002-s5-044,s1,One agent check of a mental-computation ladder is due by 31 October.
  cal-20261002-s5-045,s1,"The restyle adds a dark theme, a site-theme script, the shared title scale and pill buttons."
  cal-20261002-s5-046,s1,Calibrator adopted the shared visual style guide on 2 October.
  cal-20261002-s5-047,s1,Privacy-preserving visit counts come before retiring any visualisation.
  cal-20261002-s5-048,s1,One evening a week free of the fleet was endorsed.
  cal-20261002-s5-049,s1,The étale month was meant to be on one field alone.
  cal-20261002-s5-050,s1,The Calibrator post is a crewmate's draft.
  cal-20261002-s5-051,s1,The WebMCP call counter waits until a browser ships WebMCP.
  cal-20261002-s5-052,s1,The digest is agent-written.
  cal-20261002-s5-053,s1,The next structural tool aims at practising engineers.
  cal-20261002-s5-054,s1,Post one specific hand-calculation question about beamdiag now rather than in November.
  cal-20261002-s5-055,s1,Reading one textbook chapter in full this month was endorsed over ten ports.
  cal-20261002-s5-056,s1,One evening a week free of the fleet was endorsed.
